{% extends 'dash/help/metric/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block definition %}
    <p>This card shows how Redis persists data to disk using RDB and AOF.</p>
    <p>Redis is often used as a cache only. In this case, persistence may be disabled (both RDB and AOF), as data is not meant to be kept after a restart.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block why_it_matters %}
    <p>Persistence defines how your data survives restarts or crashes. Choosing the right method impacts performance and data safety.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block how_to_read %}
    <ul class="d-flex flex-column gap-2">
        <li>
            <twig:Html:Badge:Neutral class="fs-6">RDB (Redis Database Backup)</twig:Html:Badge:Neutral>
            <p>Creates snapshots of your data at specific intervals.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Faster and lighter</li>
                <li>Can lose recent data between snapshots</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
            <twig:Html:Badge:Neutral class="fs-6">AOF (Append Only File)</twig:Html:Badge:Neutral>
            <p>Logs every write operation to a file.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Better data safety</li>
                <li>Higher disk usage and slightly lower performance</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ul>
{% endblock %}
